## Operating notes

* Take a backup of the SQLite database (and its WAL) before deploying: the migration is
  forward-only.
* There are no new metrics; refused redirects show up in `shortener_http_requests_total` with
  status `410`.
* Every redirect of a limited link performs one short write transaction. The redirect rate limiter
  still runs first.

## Limitations

* The limit counts granted redirects: every `302` counts, including link-preview bots and
  repeat visits of the same person. It is not a unique-visitor limit.
* The limit cannot be changed or reset after creation (the API has no update endpoint); that
  immutability is what allows the cache to keep it.
* `click_count` is exact for links with a limit and eventually consistent for the others. The
  analytics total of a limited link (`clicks` table) can be lower than `click_count` if the click
  queue drops events.
* A consumed click is not given back if the connection breaks after the redirect was decided.
* An exhausted link costs one UPDATE (no row changes), one lookup and a `410` per request;
  caching that terminal state is a possible follow-up.
